<title>USA: RJR, Philip Morris bonds tighten on tobacco ruling.</title>
<headline>RJR, Philip Morris bonds tighten on tobacco ruling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds of tobacco firms, Philip Morris Cos Inc and RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp unit, RJ Reynolds Tobacco Co tightened five basis points after news of a favorable ruling for the industry, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;RJR and Philip Morris' bonds improved by about five basis points after news of the tobacco verdict hit the market,&quot; said one high-grade trader.</p>
<p>RJR's 8.75 percent paper due 2005 tightened to a 240 bid, 225 offer, traders said.</p>
</text>
